_X_2': 12, 'T1_X_3': 1, 'pairs': 2000, 'both_reduced': 65, 'both_basic': 1933}\nviolations: 0\nOK","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/08_reduction/check.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":378,"lines":["+#!/usr/bin/env python3","+\"\"\"Item 08 of loop0012: Theorem 3.2 (the reduction theorem), checked in the form","+`ReductionTheorem.lean` proves it, on every graph on 1..9 vertices (`nauty-geng`).","+","+Item 02 checked T1 through Algorithm X (89,972 reduced non-empty graphs to 9). This","+script replays the **Lean induction** instead — the recursion on the support size with","+its three cases — and checks every lemma the file states that no earlier item checked:","+","+  T1   for every reduced non-empty G: X ⊆ supp G, SPReduces (G − X) B (decided by a","+       search over step sequences), B ≠ ⊥, IsSPReduced B, IsBasic B,","+       |X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G); the recursion as the proof does it:","+         basic        → X = ∅, B = G;","+         disconnected → C the component of a random support vertex u, G₁ = G|C,","+                        G₂ = G|Cᶜ (both reduced, non-empty, smaller support), the","+                        recursion on both, X = X₁ ∪ X₂, B = B₁ ⊔ B₂;","+         connected    → w the two-key choice (random among ties), G* a random reduct","+                        of G − w (non-empty, reduced, smaller support, w ∉ supp G*),","+                        1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G) (S1), the recursion on G*, X = {w} ∪ X*,","+                        (G − w) − X* →* G* − X* (R4, by search), transitivity.","+  RS   restrict: ndeg (G|S) x = ndeg G x for x ∈ S, 0 otherwise, when no edge crosses","+       S (`ndeg_restrict_of_mem`, `_of_not_mem`); IsSPReduced (G|S) (`IsSPReduced.restrict`);","+       G|C ⊔ G|Cᶜ = G (`restrict_sup_restrict_compl`, item 06)","+  IS   isolateSet (G₁ ⊔ G₂) X = isolateSet G₁ X ⊔ isolateSet G₂ X (`isolateSet_sup`);","+       isolateSet G (X ∪ Y) = isolateSet G X when Y has no G-edges","+       (`isolateSet_union_of_forall_not_adj`)","+  SUP  for graphs with disjoint supports: IsSPReduced and IsBasic pass to the union","+       (`IsSPReduced.sup`, `IsBasic.sup`), f⁻ is additive (item 05), a component of","+       the union containing a G₁-vertex is a G₁-component (`supp_eq_of_agree`)","+  CP   per component C with a positive-degree vertex: cubic ⇒ compPotential = |C|/6 − 1/6","+       (`compPotential_cubic`); reduced and some degree ≥ 4 ⇒ 5/6 ≤ compPotential and","+       |C| ≥ 5 (`compPotential_ge_five_sixths`, `five_le_card_compFinset`); reduced ⇒","+       one of the two (`compPotential_cubic_or_ge_five_sixths`)","+","+Usage: nice -n 19 python3 check.py --max-n 9 --workers 8","+\"\"\"","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+import argparse","+import collections","+import json","+import os","+import random","+import subprocess","+import sys","+import time","+from fractions import Fraction","+from multiprocessing import Pool","+","+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))","+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, \"..\", \"..\", \"..\", \"..\")))","+","+from learning.edwards_mcdermid import (  # noqa: E402","+    bits, components, degrees, f_potential, fminus, g, g_prime, is_basic, is_cubic,","+    is_reduced, isolate, isolate_set, min_degree, paper_choice, parse_g6, reduce_random,","+    restrict, sp_step, step_vertices, support,","+)","+","+","+def sup(a: list[int], b: list[int]) -> list[int]:","+    return [x | y for x, y in zip(a, b)]","+","+","+def sp_reaches(G: list[int], H: list[int], limit: int = 200_000) -> bool:","+    \"\"\"`SPReduces G H`: is `H` reachable from `G` by series-parallel steps? Depth-first","+    search over the step relation with a visited set (every step empties a vertex, so","+    the depth is at most the support size).\"\"\"","+    target = tuple(H)","+    seen = {tuple(G)}","+    stack = [G]","+    while stack:","+        cur = stack.pop()","+        if tuple(cur) == target:","+            return True","+        if len(seen) > limit:","+            raise RuntimeError(\"sp_reaches: state limit\")","+        for v in step_vertices(cur):","+            nxt = sp_step(cur, v)","+            t = tuple(nxt)","+            if t not in seen:","+                seen.add(t)","+                stack.append(nxt)","+    return False","+","+","+def comp_potential(adj: list[int], C: int) -> Fraction:","+    return sum((g(adj[v].bit_count()) for v in bits(C)), Fraction(0)) - g_prime(min_degree(adj, C))","+","+","+class Checker:","+    def __init__(self, line: str, rng: random.Random) -> None:","+        self.line = line.strip()","+        self.rng = rng","+        self.cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+        self.viol: list[str] = []","+","+    def bad(self, stmt: str, detail: str) -> None:","+        self.viol.append(f\"{stmt}\\t{self.line}\\t{detail}\")","+","+    # the Lean induction, replayed","+    def recursion(self, adj: list[int], depth: int = 0) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:","+        n = len(adj)","+        full = (1 << n) - 1","+        supp = support(adj)","+        assert is_reduced(adj) and supp","+        self.cnt[\"rec_calls\"] += 1","+        if is_basic(adj):","+            self.cnt[\"case_basic\"] += 1","+            return 0, adj","+        comps = components(adj)","+        if len(comps) >= 2:","+            self.cnt[\"case_disconnected\"] += 1","+            u = self.rng.choice(list(bits(supp)))","+            C = next(c for c in comps if (c >> u) & 1)","+            Cc = full & ~C","+            G1, G2 = restrict(adj, C), restrict(adj, Cc)","+            # RS: degrees and reducedness of the halves; the union identity","+            d = degrees(adj)","+            for x in range(n):","+                if (C >> x) & 1:","+                    if G1[x].bit_count() != d[x] or G2[x].bit_count() != 0:","+                        self.bad(\"RS_deg\", f\"x={x} C={C:b}\")","+                else:","+                    if G1[x].bit_count() != 0 or G2[x].bit_count() != d[x]:","+                        self.bad(\"RS_deg\", f\"x={x} C={C:b}\")","+            self.cnt[\"RS_deg\"] += n","+            if not (is_reduced(G1) and is_reduced(G2)):","+                self.bad(\"RS_reduced\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+            if sup(G1, G2) != adj:","+                self.bad(\"RS_sup\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+            if not (any(G1) and any(G2)):","+                self.bad(\"RS_nonempty\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+            if not (support(G1) < supp and support(G2) < supp and support(G1) != supp and support(G2) != supp):","+                self.bad(\"RS_smaller\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+            self.cnt[\"RS\"] += 1","+            X1, B1 = self.recursion(G1, depth + 1)","+            X2, B2 = self.recursion(G2, depth + 1)","+            # the sides stay inside their halves","+            if X1 & ~C or X2 & C:","+                self.bad(\"D_sides\", f\"X1={X1:b} X2={X2:b} C={C:b}\")","+            if support(B1) & ~C or support(B2) & C:","+                self.bad(\"D_Bsides\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+            # IS: the isolateSet identities","+            lhs = isolate_set(adj, X1 | X2)","+            rhs = sup(isolate_set(G1, X1), isolate_set(G2, X2))","+            if lhs != rhs:","+                self.bad(\"IS\", f\"X1={X1:b} X2={X2:b}\")","+            if isolate_set(sup(G1, G2), X1 | X2) != sup(isolate_set(G1, X1 | X2), isolate_set(G2, X1 | X2)):","+                self.bad(\"IS_sup\", f\"X1={X1:b} X2={X2:b}\")","+            if isolate_set(G1, X1 | X2) != isolate_set(G1, X1) or isolate_set(G2, X1 | X2) != isolate_set(G2, X2):","+                self.bad(\"IS_union\", f\"X1={X1:b} X2={X2:b}\")","+            self.cnt[\"IS\"] += 1","+            # SUP: the union of the two basic reducts","+            B = sup(B1, B2)","+            if support(B1) & support(B2):","+                self.bad(\"SUP_disjoint\", \"\")","+            if not is_reduced(B):","+                self.bad(\"SUP_reduced\", \"\")","+            if not is_basic(B):","+                self.bad(\"SUP_basic\", \"\")","+            if fminus(B) != fminus(B1) + fminus(B2):","+                self.bad(\"SUP_fminus\", \"\")","+            if fminus(adj) != fminus(G1) + fminus(G2):","+                self.bad(\"SUP_fminusG\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+            # a component of B containing a B1-vertex is a B1-component","+            for K in components(B):","+                v = next(iter(bits(K)))","+                side = B1 if B1[v] else B2","+                KK = next(c for c in components(side) if (c >> v) & 1)","+                if KK != K:","+                    self.bad(\"SUP_comp\", f\"K={K:b}\")","+                self.cnt[\"SUP_comp\"] += 1","+            self.cnt[\"SUP\"] += 1","+            # the lifted reductions (R5), by search","+            if not sp_reaches(sup(isolate_set(G1, X1), isolate_set(G2, X2)), sup(B1, isolate_set(G2, X2))):","+                self.bad(\"D_R5a\", f\"X1={X1:b}\")","+            if not sp_reaches(sup(isolate_set(G2, X2), B1), sup(B2, B1)):","+                self.bad(\"D_R5b\", f\"X2={X2:b}\")","+            self.cnt[\"R5\"] += 2","+            return X1 | X2, B","+        # connected, not basic","+        self.cnt[\"case_connected\"] += 1","+        _, chosen, D = paper_choice(adj)","+        w = self.rng.choice(chosen)","+        Gp = isolate(adj, w)","+        Gs = reduce_random(Gp, self.rng)","+        if D < 4:","+            self.bad(\"C_delta\", f\"w={w} Δ={D}\")","+        if not any(Gs):","+            self.bad(\"C_nonempty\", f\"w={w}\")","+        if not is_reduced(Gs):","+            self.bad(\"C_reduced\", f\"w={w}\")","+        ss = support(Gs)","+        if not (ss & ~supp == 0 and ss != supp and not (ss >> w) & 1):","+            self.bad(\"C_smaller\", f\"w={w}\")","+        if not 1 + fminus(Gs) <= fminus(adj):","+            self.bad(\"C_S1\", f\"w={w}\")","+        self.cnt[\"C\"] += 1","+        Xs, B = self.recursion(Gs, depth + 1)","+        if (Xs >> w) & 1:","+            self.bad(\"C_wX\", f\"w={w} Xs={Xs:b}\")","+        if Xs & ~ss:","+            self.bad(\"C_Xsupp\", f\"w={w} Xs={Xs:b}\")","+        X = Xs | (1 << w)","+        if isolate_set(adj, X) != isolate_set(Gp, Xs):","+            self.bad(\"C_insert\", f\"w={w} Xs={Xs:b}\")","+        # R4 by search: (G − w) − X* →* G* − X*","+        if not sp_reaches(isolate_set(Gp, Xs), isolate_set(Gs, Xs)):","+            self.bad(\"C_R4\", f\"w={w} Xs={Xs:b}\")","+        self.cnt[\"R4\"] += 1","+        if not Xs.bit_count() + 1 + fminus(B) <= fminus(adj):","+            self.bad(\"C_ineq\", f\"w={w}\")","+        return X, B","+","+    def run(self, adj: list[int]) -> None:","+        n = len(adj)","+        self.cnt[\"graphs\"] += 1","+        d = degrees(adj)","+        supp = support(adj)","+        # CP: the per-component statements, on every graph","+        for C in components(adj):","+            self.cnt[\"CP_components\"] += 1","+            cp = comp_potential(adj, C)","+            N = C.bit_count()","+            if is_cubic(adj, C):","+                self.cnt[\"CP_cubic\"] += 1","+                if cp != Fraction(N, 6) - Fraction(1, 6):","+                    self.bad(\"CP_cubic\", f\"C={C:b} cp={cp}\")","+            if all(d[v] >= 3 for v in bits(C)):","+                self.cnt[\"CP_reduced\"] += 1","+                if any(d[v] >= 4 for v in bits(C)):","+                    self.cnt[\"CP_noncubic\"] += 1","+                    if not cp >= Fraction(5, 6):","+                        self.bad(\"CP_floor\", f\"C={C:b} cp={cp}\")","+                    if N < 5:","+                        self.bad(\"CP_five\", f\"C={C:b} N={N}\")","+                if not (cp == Fraction(N, 6) - Fraction(1, 6) or cp >= Fraction(5, 6)):","+                    self.bad(\"CP_dichotomy\", f\"C={C:b} cp={cp}\")","+            if cp < 0:","+                self.bad(\"CP_nonneg\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+        # RS on the component of the lowest support vertex (any graph)","+        if supp:","+            u = (supp & -supp).bit_length() - 1","+            C = next(c for c in components(adj) if (c >> u) & 1)","+            G1 = restrict(adj, C)","+            for x in range(n):","+                want = d[x] if (C >> x) & 1 else 0","+                if G1[x].bit_count() != want:","+                    self.bad(\"RS_deg_any\", f\"x={x} C={C:b}\")","+            if is_reduced(adj) and not is_reduced(G1):","+                self.bad(\"RS_reduced_any\", f\"C={C:b}\")","+            self.cnt[\"RS_any\"] += 1","+        # IS on random X, Y with Y off the support","+        full = (1 << n) - 1","+        X = self.rng.randrange(1 << n)","+        off = full & ~supp","+        Y = self.rng.randrange(1 << n) & off","+        if isolate_set(adj, X | Y) != isolate_set(adj, X):","+            self.bad(\"IS_union_any\", f\"X={X:b} Y={Y:b}\")","+        self.cnt[\"IS_any\"] += 1","+        # T1 as the proof does it","+        if is_reduced(adj) and supp:","+            self.cnt[\"T1\"] += 1","+            X, B = self.recursion(adj)","+            if X & ~supp:","+                self.bad(\"T1_supp\", f\"X={X:b}\")","+            if not any(B):","+                self.bad(\"T1_empty\", f\"X={X:b}\")","+            if not is_reduced(B):","+                self.bad(\"T1_reduced\", f\"X={X:b}\")","+            if not is_basic(B):","+                self.bad(\"T1_basic\", f\"X={X:b}\")","+            if not X.bit_count() + fminus(B) <= fminus(adj):","+                self.bad(\"T1_ineq\", f\"X={X:b} |X|+f⁻(B)={X.bit_count() + fminus(B)} f⁻(G)={fminus(adj)}\")","+            if not sp_reaches(isolate_set(adj, X), B):","+                self.bad(\"T1_reduces\", f\"X={X:b}\")","+            self.cnt[f\"T1_X_{X.bit_count()}\"] += 1","+","+","+def one(args: tuple[int, str]) -> dict:","+    idx, line = args","+    n, adj = parse_g6(line)","+    ck = Checker(line, random.Random(idx * 7_919 + n))","+    ck.run(adj)","+    return {\"cnt\": ck.cnt, \"viol\": ck.viol}","+","+","+def pair(args: tuple[int, str, str]) -> dict:","+    \"\"\"SUP on two random graphs embedded on disjoint vertex sets.\"\"\"","+    idx, l1, l2 = args","+    n1, a1 = parse_g6(l1)","+    n2, a2 = parse_g6(l2)","+    n = n1 + n2","+    G1 = a1 + [0] * n2","+    G2 = [0] * n1 + [a << n1 for a in a2]","+    G = sup(G1, G2)","+    cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+    viol: list[str] = []","+    cnt[\"pairs\"] += 1","+    r1, r2, r = is_reduced(G1), is_reduced(G2), is_reduced(G)","+    b1, b2, b = is_basic(G1), is_basic(G2), is_basic(G)","+    if r1 and r2 and not r:","+        viol.append(f\"SUP_reduced_pair\\t{l1.strip()} {l2.strip()}\")","+    if b1 and b2 and not b:","+        viol.append(f\"SUP_basic_pair\\t{l1.strip()} {l2.strip()}\")","+    if r != (r1 and r2):","+        cnt[\"reduced_converse_fails\"] += 1","+    if b != (b1 and b2):","+        cnt[\"basic_converse_fails\"] += 1","+    if fminus(G) != fminus(G1) + fminus(G2):","+        viol.append(f\"SUP_fminus_pair\\t{l1.strip()} {l2.strip()}\")","+    cnt[\"both_reduced\"] += int(r1 and r2)","+    cnt[\"both_basic\"] += int(b1 and b2)","+    return {\"cnt\": cnt, \"viol\": viol}","+","+","+def geng(n: int) -> list[str]:","+    return subprocess.run([\"nauty-geng\", \"-q\", str(n)], capture_output=True, text=True,","+                          check=True).stdout.splitlines()","+","+","+def main() -> None:","+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()","+    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=9)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=8)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--pairs\", type=int, default=20000)","+    a = ap.parse_args()","+    log = open(f\"{HERE}/check.log\", \"w\")","+","+    def say(s: str = \"\") -> None:","+        print(s, flush=True)","+        log.write(s + \"\\n\")","+        log.flush()","+","+    say(f\"# item 08 brute-force check, {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC', time.gmtime())}, \"","+        f\"every graph on 1..{a.max_n} vertices (nauty-geng), {a.workers} workers; \"","+        f\"{a.pairs} random disjoint pairs\")","+    total: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+    per_n: dict[int, dict] = {}","+    violations: list[str] = []","+    t0 = time.time()","+    rng = random.Random(2026_11_02)","+    pool_lines: list[str] = []","+    with Pool(a.workers) as pool:","+        for n in range(1, a.max_n + 1):","+            lines = geng(n)","+            if n <= 5:","+                pool_lines += lines","+            cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+            for res in pool.imap_unordered(one, list(enumerate(lines)), chunksize=64):","+                cnt.update(res[\"cnt\"])","+                violations += res[\"viol\"]","+            per_n[n] = dict(cnt)","+            total.update(cnt)","+            say(f\"n={n}: {len(lines)} graphs, T1 on {cnt['T1']} reduced non-empty; recursion calls \"","+                f\"{cnt['rec_calls']} (basic/disconnected/connected = {cnt['case_basic']}/\"","+                f\"{cnt['case_disconnected']}/{cnt['case_connected']}); components {cnt['CP_components']} \"","+                f\"(cubic {cnt['CP_cubic']}, reduced non-cubic {cnt['CP_noncubic']}); \"","+                f\"violations so far {len(violations)}; {time.time() - t0:.0f} s\")","+        # random disjoint pairs from graphs on ≤ 5 vertices (so the union has ≤ 10)","+        jobs = [(i, rng.choice(pool_lines), rng.choice(pool_lines)) for i in range(a.pairs)]","+        pcnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+        for res in pool.imap_unordered(pair, jobs, chunksize=64):","+            pcnt.update(res[\"cnt\"])","+            violations += res[\"viol\"]","+        total.update(pcnt)","+        say(f\"pairs: {dict(pcnt)}; violations so far {len(violations)}; {time.time() - t0:.0f} s\")","+    say(f\"TOTAL: {dict(total)}\")","+    say(f\"violations: {len(violations)}\")","+    